1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Mary Hobson was an English woman who had a successful life, but always felt a deep love for literature.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
One day, while recovering in the hospital from surgery at the age of 56,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
she read a translated poem by Russian author Alexander Pushkin,

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
and it moved her so deeply she decided she had to read it in the original Russian.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Despite never learning the language before, she started studying it seriously.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000
It was slow and difficult, learning a new alphabet, new grammar, and completely foreign sounds,

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
but she persisted.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
She eventually became fluent in Russian, went on to earn a PhD in Russian literature,

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
and even became a respected translator of Russian works into English.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000
She received awards from Russia for her contributions to culture and literature.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
All of this started after most people think they're too old to learn.

12
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
It's never too late to start learning.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Age is not a barrier, only doubt is.

14
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:03,000
If you have curiosity and determination, you can open new doors at any stage in life.

15
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Want one about someone who overcame failure through learning?

